{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520991-limit-mechanics-post-sidereals","id":1520991,"title":"Limit Mechanics Post-Sidereals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-19T16:03:30-07:00","id":1520991,"title":"Limit Mechanics Post-Sidereals","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If you have access to the Sidereal Kickstarter, you\u2019ve probably seen their version of the Great Curse: Celestial Hubris. And I am a <i>huge</i> fan.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Now, I admit that I was already a huge Sidereal fan, but before, I always thought of the Limit Mechanic as this annoying hanger on, this necessary evil that was required to model your status as a tragic hero, both propelled and doomed by your great passions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But I found the setup provided by Celestial Hubris to be very engaging. There\u2019s this whole push and pull between keeping your limit low and your Willpower high, while at the same time encouraging players to engage with Sidereals in their role as Viziers.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(I would like to note that the ability to recover Willpower is a lot more significant in 3<sup>rd</sup> Edition since your mote pool calculation is no longer derived from your Willpower, meaning that players who like to indulge in occasional Min-Maxxing [like yours truly] aren\u2019t tempted to max out the stat ASAP.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I understand that this is, in part, because the Great Curse does not fall upon Sidereals as heavily as it does for, as an example, the Solars, so it wouldn\u2019t make as much sense for them to have a way to lose Limit (more) easily.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But now I wonder: in what ways can the Limit mechanic for other Exalted to be adjusted to 